---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_70",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 70,
  "text": "<p> [[188.16]] <b>60b. LEIBNIZ AN MAGNUS HESENTHALER</p>\n<p> [[188.17]] [Mai ─ Oktober 1671.] [60a.]</b></p>\n<p> [[189.6]] Quia licuit mihi beneficio tuo majore, quam antea solitus eram, in <b>Comenii</b> scriptis\n[[189.7]] animi attentione versari, judicium meum qualecunque, quod flagitas, ingenue perscribam. Et\n[[189.8]] primum agnosco profundiores paullo cogitationes voluisse, quam prima specie apparent. Vellem\n[[189.9]] ad particularia se demisisset magis. Neque enim dubito ingentem ei rerum apparatum tot\n[[189.10]] annorum studio comportatum praesto fuisse, cum praesertim ipsummet alicubi et rationibus et\n[[189.11]] exemplo suo excerpendi studium commendare videam. <b>Didactica</b> ejus in summa valde\n[[189.12]] probo, nec moveor illis quae in sua <i>methodo</i> <b>Beccherus</b> objicit. Becchero videtur vocabula\n[[189.13]] naturali ordine digesta quidem, sed disjuncta separataque, nec in continuitatem sermonis\n[[189.14]] colligata, exhibenda discentibus esse. Mihi contra videtur, nihil lucis nihil jucunditatis inesse\n[[189.15]] simplici vocabulorum congeriei, utcunque ordinatae, quod ex ipso Beccheriano specimine satis\n[[189.16]] apparet. <b>Comenio igitur prorsus assentior, Januam</b> <b>Linguarum et Encyclopaediolam</b>\n[[189.17]] <b>debere esse idem.</b> Illud tamen diffiteri non possum in hac philosophiae luce rem\n[[189.18]] paullo aliter instituendam, quam illis temporibus potuit Comenius. Quaeres, <b>quid</b> <b>Encyclopaediolam\n[[189.19]] complecti debere credam?</b> Ego vero ad eam pertinere puto <b>primum</b>\n[[189.20]] definitiones vocabulorum crebriorum et insigniorum, et ex his deducta theoremata et problemata\n[[189.21]] insignioris usus, eaque in moralibus adagio aliquo dictoque Sapientum aut historia\n[[189.22]] memorabili vestita aut potius explicata: <b>deinde</b> experimenta naturae vulgariora, <b>denique</b>\n[[189.23]] compendium Historiae et Geographiae tum universalis, tum inprimis hodiernae. Videtur mihi\n[[189.24]] Hornius hac inprimis fine postrema aliquot opuscula sua publicasse, quem ego, quicquid etiam\n[[189.25]] dicant delicatiores, non omnino contemno, melioribus tamen opus esse agnosco. Encyclopaediolam\n[[189.26]] autem his contractis constare vel hinc apparet, quod Encyclopaedia integris absolvitur.\n[[189.27]] <b>Est enim</b> utique <b>Encyclopaedia</b> <b>Systema omnium,</b> <b>quousque licet, propositionum\n[[189.28]] verarum, utilium, hactenus cognitarum.</b> Omnes autem propositiones aut\n[[189.29]] singulares sunt aut universales, quanquam dentur singulares quiddam universitatis tenentes, ut\n[[189.30]] propositiones de corporibus coelestibus ob constantiam cursus, quemadmodum contra dantur\n[[189.31]] universales singularibus accedentes, quae scilicet inductione sunt fabricatae. Singulares universae\n[[190.1]] sunt pars aut historiae aut Geographiae universalis, aut potius utriusque, tractant enim de\n[[190.2]] iis quae certo tempore locoque evenere. Propositiones universales vel <b>demonstratione</b> vel\n[[190.3]] <b>inductione</b> constitutae sunt, id est vel ratione vel sensu. <b>Demonstratione</b> cognitae sunt\n[[190.4]] propositiones, quae pendent ex definitionibus vocabulorum, seu claris distinctisque ideis rerum,\n[[190.5]] quales sunt omnes arithmeticae, geometricae, logicae, metaphysicae, magnaque pars earum,\n[[190.6]] quae ad moralia scientiamque civilem ac jurisprudentiam naturalem pertinent; quarum omnium\n[[190.7]] clavis in definitionibus continetur. Cum enim <b>nihil sit aliud demonstratio</b> <b>quam combinatio\n[[190.8]] definitionum,</b> ut in <i>arte combinatoria</i> ostendi, manifestum est, qui claras quasdam\n[[190.9]] ac lucidas definitiones vocum habet (quales Plato in dialogis passim, Aristoteles, Euclides\n[[190.10]] caeterique mathematici; JC^#'t^#'i veteres in pandectis, Cujacius, Campanella, Cartesius, Hobbius, et\n[[190.11]] saepissime Ritschelius dare solent) eum innumera theoremata solius Analyseos ope (ut in\n[[190.12]] arithmeticis Diophantus et Cardanus, in Geometricis Vieta et Cartesius, at in mechanicis et\n[[190.13]] civilibus hactenus docuit nemo) eruere, et problema datum solvere, aut ostendere impossibilitatem\n[[190.14]] posse. Quo negotio cum apex humanae scientiae contineatur, efficiam spero, ut quae\n[[190.15]] aliquando <b>de arte combinatoria</b> Lullianorum exerrationibus depravata et infamata <b>pene\n[[190.16]] puerilibus annis orsus</b> sum, fructu aliquo exitum sortiantur. <b>Inductione</b> cognitae sunt\n[[190.17]] propositiones medicorum, chemicorum, astronomorum pleraeque omnes aut saltem fundamentales.\n[[190.18]] Denique dantur propositiones mixtae ex theorematibus et observationibus inter se combinatis\n[[190.19]] deductae. Sed quo feror? Volui haec eo tantum consilio huc afferre, ut ostenderem, non\n[[190.20]] posse perfectam Encyclopaediam, aut Encyclopaediolam fieri, nisi omnium potissimorum\n[[190.21]] vocabulorum definitionibus, omnibus experimentis artium liberalium pariter et mechanicarum\n[[190.22]] fundamentalibus, utilioribus, denique Historia universali temporum locorumque distinctissima\n[[190.23]] summaria, collectis et digestis. Unde omnia accedentibus tantum artibus combinatoria et\n[[190.24]] analytica, seu synthetica et resolutoria, quarum illa inventionis haec judicii est, proprio ingenio\n[[190.25]] suppleri possunt; quanquam auctis interim experimentis, Historia et geographia, ipsa quoque\n[[190.26]] Encyclopaediae suppellex perpetuo augeatur. Sed et Historiae et Observationes particulares,\n[[190.27]] quae nihil cum publicis negotii habent, ut Sectio anatomica monstri cujusdam, ubi parum refert\n[[190.28]] quo loco et tempore contigerit, rectius velut materia inductionum ab historia et Geographia ad\n[[190.29]] experimenta transferuntur. Haec mihi nuperrime circa Comeniana destinata consiliumque praeclarum\n[[190.30]] Encyclopaediae perficiendae in mentem venere aut rediere. </p>\n",
  "number": "60b.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN MAGNUS HESENTHALER",
  "date": "[Mai ─ Oktober 1671.] [60a.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:60b. LEIBNIZ AN MAGNUS HESENTHALER [Mai ─ Oktober 1671.] [60a.] Quia licuit mihi beneficio tuo majore, quam antea solitus eram, in Comenii scriptis animi attentione versari, judicium meum qualecunque, quod flagitas, ingenue perscribam. Et primum agnosco profundiores paullo cogitationes voluisse, qua...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>